From 21fe65264b89453e95b8114b700e312b46e1a722 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:41:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(power-supply): bind direct charging to its session and
 suspend lifecycle

Check both cell temperature extremes. Keep each direct-charge operation tied to its original GLINK and connector generation, and confirm the stage has stopped before restoring source policy. Retry failed stops without releasing the power supply.

Use a freezable policy worker and a managed supplier link to stop policy before the stage suspends. Block suspend on failed stop, restart polling on resume, and quiesce policy during shutdown.

Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/piano_mca.c | 226 +++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 173 insertions(+), 53 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/piano_mca.c b/drivers/power/supply/piano_mca.c
index 799a14527..e78ee14f9 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/piano_mca.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/piano_mca.c
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
 #include <linux/hex.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
+#include <linux/pm.h>
 #include <linux/power_supply.h>
 #include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/random.h>
